DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((sqrt((ln(x)))))");
$fun_1 = Formula("cos((ln(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-8, -5, -2, -1, 6, 10} U ({-9, 0, 6})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-9, 0, 6} U {-9, 0, 6} U ({-8, -5, -2, -1, 6, 10} U {-9, 0, 6})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(({-4, -2, 7, 10} U {-4, -2, 7, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-4, -2, 7, 10})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-4, -2, 7, 10})) U {-5, -4, -3, 2, 6}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-4, -2, 7, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-5, -4, -3, 2, 6}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-5, -4, -3, 2, 6}))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-4, -2, 7, 10} - {-5, -4, -3, 2, 6})");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`8*13+14`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(118.),width=>6}
---

[`14+8`] is equal to [_____]{Real(22.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-5, -4, -3, 2, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{-4, -2, 7, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{-5, 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`((B \cup B \cap B) \cap B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap A \cap (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, 0, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 1\}`]
- [`C = \{-8, -5, -2, -1, 6, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup A \cup (C \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -3, -6, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, 10, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -3, 4, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<0, 10, 7>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, -6, -8>") . Compute("<0, 10, 7>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 4, -5>") x Compute("<0, 10, 7>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, 10, 7>") . Compute("<-3, -6, -8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, -6, -8>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, 4, -5>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, 9, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, 2, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -6, 1, 4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 9, -2>") . Compute("<-6, 1, 4>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 9, -2>") . Compute("<-4, 2, 4>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, 1, 4>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 2, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>4)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
